\nL166:   * Method Chaining Support: Write more concise and expressive code with method chaining\nL167:   * Improved Rust API: Better trait design with standard operator overloading\nL168:   * Enhanced Program API: Reorganized Program module with better type safety\nL169:   * Backward Compatibility: Comprehensive migration guides for v3 to v4 transition\nL170:   * Post Quantum: Implemented a NIST FIPS203 (ML-KEM) protocol on CUDA, fully open-source\nL171:   * Lattice Based Cryptography: Add support for Lattice based cryptography, with integer ring support and a full LaBRADOR prover (soon announced)\nL172: ## 🔄 Breaking Changes\nL173: \nL174: ### C++ API Changes\nL175: \nL176: #### Field Arithmetic Operations\nL177: \nL178: All field operations have been converted from static methods to instance methods\nL179: Check the 【76†migration page†dev.ingonyama.com】 for more details\nL180: \nL181: ### Rust API Changes\nL182: \nL183: #### Arithmetic Trait Redesign\nL184: \nL185: The `FieldImpl` trait has been deprecated and split into focused, orthogonal traits\nL186: ## What's Changed\nL187:   * Negacyclic NTT for polynomial rings by 【77†@yshekel】 in 【78†#930】\nL188:   * Update README.md by 【79†@Shalmoni】 in 【80†#931】\nL189:   * Fixed devdocs link licensing by 【79†@Shalmoni】 in 【81†#933】\nL190:   * Fix collab instructions for version mismatch error by 【82†@jeremyfelder】 in 【83†#935】\nL191:   * Feat: generate JL-projection matrix rows by 【77†@yshekel】 in 【84†#936】\nL192:   * Curve Montgomery Conversion Fix for Host Memory by 【85†@emirsoyturk】 in 【86†#938】\nL193:   * [FIX] Invalid memory access causes hang by 【82†@jeremyfelder】 in 【87†#939】\nL194:   * PQC ML-KEM by 【88†@nonam3e】 and 【89†@dorshmil】 in 【90†#932】\nL195:   * Add PQC documentation to 3.9.0 by 【91†@LeonHibnik】 in 【92†#940】\nL196:   * Changed broken link on readme by 【79†@Shalmoni】 in 【93†#942】\nL197:   * [FEAT] Rust Polynomial-Ring trait and NegacyclicNTT by 【77†@yshekel】 in 【94†#943】\nL198:   * [FEAT] Decompose Polynomial-rings by 【77†@yshekel】 in 【95†#945】\nL199:   * [FEAT] JL-projection Rust wrapper by 【77†@yshekel】 in 【96†#949】\nL200:   * [FEAT] MatMul API by 【97†@lnm-at-work】 in 【98†#871】\nL201:   * [FEAT] Expose Sumcheck protocol challenge vector by 【91†@LeonHibnik】 in 【99†#946】\nL202:   * Timur/pqc go wrappers by 【88†@nonam3e】 in 【100†#944】\nL203:   * [FEAT] Add flattening utilities for polynomial slices into scalar slices by 【77†@yshekel】 in 【101†#952】\nL204:   * [CI] Separate testing by feature by 【82†@jeremyfelder】 in 【102†#913】\nL205:   * [FEAT] Add reinterpretation utilities and polynomial vector operations by 【77†@yshekel】 in 【103†#954】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn3view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://oraclizer.io/ss-gkr/docs/concepts/how-gkr-works/\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://oraclizer.io/ss-gkr/docs/concepts/how-gkr-works/: Cache miss"
